q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 10 Tf 13 TL (2. What is exception handling in Python?) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 604.2047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 16.4 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 12.8 TL (Exception handling is used to handle errors in a program. It helps the program to show a proper message instead of) Tj T* (stopping suddenly. Python uses try and except for this.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 586.2047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 10 Tf 13 TL (3. What is the purpose of the finally block in exception handling?) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 554.6047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 16.4 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 12.8 TL (The finally block is used for code which should run at the end. It runs whether an error occurs or not. It is often used for) Tj T* (closing files.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 536.6047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 10 Tf 13 TL (4. What is logging in Python?) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 505.0047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 16.4 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 12.8 TL (Logging means saving information about what is happening in a program. It is useful for finding errors and checking the) Tj T* (working of a program.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 487.0047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 10 Tf 13 TL (5. What is the significance of the __del__ method in Python?) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 455.4047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 16.4 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 12.8 TL -0.037141 Tw (The __del__ method is related to deleting an object. It can be called when an object is going to be removed. It can be used) Tj T* 0 Tw (for cleanup, but it should not be depended on for important cleanup work.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 437.4047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 10 Tf 13 TL (6. What is the difference between import and from ... import in Python?) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 405.8047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 16.4 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 12.8 TL (import imports a module. We use the module name to use its functions. from ... import imports a particular function or) Tj T* (object from a module.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 387.8047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 10 Tf 13 TL (7. How can you handle multiple exceptions in Python?) Tj T* ET
