q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 10 Tf 13 TL (9. What is the difference between multithreading and multiprocessing?) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 282.6047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 16.4 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 12.8 TL (Multithreading uses more than one thread in a program. Multiprocessing uses more than one process. Threads are useful) Tj T* (for I/O tasks and processes can be useful for CPU-heavy tasks.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 264.6047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 10 Tf 13 TL (10. What are the advantages of using logging in a program?) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 48.51969 233.0047 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 16.4 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 12.8 TL (Logging helps to find errors and understand the program. It keeps a record of important events. It is also useful when we) Tj T* (need to check a program later.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
